<title>GERMANY: German CDU wants capital gains tax on stock sales.</title>
<headline>German CDU wants capital gains tax on stock sales.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl's Christian Democrats (CDU) said on Tuesday they want to tighten rules on taxing capital gains on stock and real estate sales.</p>
<p>The party said that as part of a comprehensive tax reform Germany should tax all such asset sales and not just speculative sales of assets held less than six months.</p>
<p>Commenting on how appreciation of real estate would be handled, the party suggested that an exception would be made for primary residences.</p>
<p>The proposals are contained in a party position paper on the tax reform presented to journalists at a news conference.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
